WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.122
M-22-09 is the only one of the
four that sets dated actions

2
00:00:04.122 --> 00:00:07.337
for the program itself, and it
isn't limited to the cloud.

3
00:00:07.337 --> 00:00:10.813
It also addresses on-premises
and hybrid systems.

4
00:00:10.813 --> 00:00:13.187
By pillar, the actions are specific.

5
00:00:13.187 --> 00:00:15.941
Identity: centralized identity management,

6
00:00:15.941 --> 00:00:19.885
and phishing-resistant multi-factor
authentication for staff,

7
00:00:19.885 --> 00:00:24.499
contractors and partners, which means
agency systems stop supporting SMS

8
00:00:24.499 --> 00:00:29.038
and voice codes, one-time codes and
push notifications for routine access.

9
00:00:29.038 --> 00:00:34.044
Devices: reliable asset inventories
through CISA's Continuous Diagnostics

10
00:00:34.044 --> 00:00:39.050
and Mitigation program, and endpoint
detection and response deployed widely.

11
00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:44.324
Networks: encrypted DNS, HTTPS for
all web and API traffic, and a plan

12
00:00:44.324 --> 00:00:50.462
for environmental isolation, moving
away from one broad enterprise network.

13
00:00:50.462 --> 00:00:55.845
Applications: dedicated security testing,
a public vulnerability disclosure program,

14
00:00:55.845 --> 00:00:59.164
and at least one internal
FISMA Moderate application

15
00:00:59.164 --> 00:01:02.187
made fully operational
over the public internet.

16
00:01:02.187 --> 00:01:07.000
Data: initial automation of data
categorization, and comprehensive logging.

17
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.163
Its fiscal 2024 deadlines have passed.

18
00:01:10.163 --> 00:01:14.791
OMB hasn't rescinded it: its
memoranda index lists no rescission,

19
00:01:14.791 --> 00:01:17.062
and the memo is still published.

20
00:01:17.062 --> 00:01:19.812
A passed deadline
doesn't retire an action.

21
00:01:19.812 --> 00:01:22.890
Agencies are now measured
against these actions as

22
00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:25.825
an existing obligation
rather than a target date.

23
00:01:25.825 --> 00:01:27.113
There's one adjustment.

24
00:01:27.113 --> 00:01:33.511
The logging action points to M-21-31,
which M-26-14 rescinded on May 22, 2026,

25
00:01:33.511 --> 00:01:41.212
replacing its tiers with a risk-based approach
and a Logging Reference Architecture.

26
00:01:41.212 --> 00:01:46.262
CISA published that architecture on
August 20, 2026, and the memo gives

27
00:01:46.262 --> 00:01:51.225
agencies 90 days from its release
for their first Agency Logging Plan.

28
00:01:51.225 --> 00:01:53.513
That's the decision with the nearest date.

29
00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:58.226
The CISO decides how the Agency Logging
Plan covers Zero Trust telemetry,

30
00:01:58.226 --> 00:02:01.951
including the hosts and accounts
that run the assessments.

31
00:02:01.951 --> 00:02:05.930
It's due 90 days after August 20, 2026.
